## Grammar Rules 4 & 5 Integration

### Grammar Rules 4 (copula, kinship, enumeratives, ka particle)

Applied via:
```python
from language_rules_gr4 import apply_gr4_rules

text = apply_gr4_rules(text, direction="en->lun")
```

**What it fixes**:
- Copula constructions (ni-, ku-)
- Kinship term agreement (ise wange → isange)
- Enumerative forms (abakulu → abatuku)
- Ka particle usage (ka + adjective = permissive)

### Grammar Rules 5 (locatives, reversive, objectival concord)

Applied via:
```python
from language_rules_gr5 import apply_gr5_rules

text = apply_gr5_rules(text, direction="en->lun")
```

**What it fixes**:
- Locative adverbial suffixes (-mu/-ho/-yo)
- Reversive verbs (-i suffix)
- Objectival concords (gu-, ki-, bi-, etc.)

